# Firebase Read Strategy

## Hard Limits (Spark Plan — free)

| Resource | Daily Limit | Resets at midnight Pacific |
|----------|-------------|---------------------------|
| Reads | 50,000/day | Exceeding = shut off until next day |
| Writes | 20,000/day | |
| Deletes | 20,000/day | |
| Storage | 1 GiB | |
| Egress | 10 GiB/month | |

GitHub Actions cleanup overhead: ~2,400 reads/day
Available for app users: **~47,600 reads/day**

## Sync Parameters (SyncManager.kt)

| Parameter | Value | Why |
|-----------|-------|-----|
| `MIN_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS` | 10 min | Pull-to-refresh cooldown — prevents spamming reads |
| `BATCH_SIZE` | 50 | Matches ~50-80 new articles per 30-min GitHub Actions run |
| `MAX_SYNC_CAP` | 300 | Full sync on first open — rich content across all categories |
| `OLD_DATA_TTL_MS` | 7 days | Stale threshold for smart delete |
| `MIN_CATEGORY_RETENTION` | 100 | Categories with <100 articles never get pruned |
| `CATEGORY_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS` | 24 hours | Categories change rarely |
| `AUTO_REFRESH_INTERVAL_MS` | 30 min | Matches GitHub Actions schedule — silent, in viewModelScope |

## Quality-Aware Sync Flow

Every sync fetches **high quality first**, then fills the gap with low quality:

```
Step 1: Fetch up to LIMIT articles WHERE quality = "high"
Step 2: If highCount < LIMIT → fetch (LIMIT - highCount) WHERE quality = "low"
Step 3: Save all to Room with quality tag
```

- Incremental sync: LIMIT = BATCH_SIZE (50)
- Full sync: LIMIT = MAX_SYNC_CAP (300)
- Worst case: +1 extra Firebase query per sync (gap-fill). Typical case: 0 extra reads.
- Requires composite Firestore index: `quality ASC + publishedAt DESC` on `news_articles`

## Seven Safety Guards

1. **Pull-to-refresh cooldown** = 10 min — skip if lastSync < 10 min ago, use Room cache
2. **Max sync cap** = 300 — only on first open or after 24h gap
3. **Incremental batch** = 50 — keeps each sync lightweight
4. **Auto-refresh** = 30 min — silent, foreground only (viewModelScope)
5. **Category sync** = once/day — ~18 reads instead of 18 per open
6. **Smart Room retention** — only delete 7-day-old articles from categories with 100+ articles
7. **Quality-first fetch** — high quality articles always fetched first, low quality only fills gaps

## Read Budget Per User Per Day

| User Type | Session | Pulls | Auto-refreshes | Reads/Day |
|-----------|---------|-------|----------------|-----------|
| Light (15 min) | 15 min | 1 | 0 | ~78 |
| Normal (1 hr) | 1 hr | 2 | 1 | ~168 |
| Heavy (3-4 hr) | 3 hr | 5 | 5 | ~438 |
| Power (8 hr) | 8 hr | 10 | 16 | ~828 |
| First-time (full) | 30 min | 1 | 0 | ~348 |

## DAU Capacity on Free Tier

| Scenario | DAU |
|----------|-----|
| All light | 610 |
| All normal | 283 |
| All heavy | 108 |
| Realistic mix (60% light, 30% normal, 10% heavy) | **~363** |
| Early stage (10-20 users) | ~13% of limit |

## Zero Firebase Reads Operations

- Browse / scroll → Room PagingSource
- Switch category → Room PagingSource
- Load more (pagination) → Room PagingSource
- Search → Room FTS query

## Rules for Any Code Change

- NEVER add a new Firebase read path without calculating its impact on the daily budget
- NEVER reduce sync intervals below current values without recalculating DAU capacity
- NEVER remove or weaken any of the 7 safety guards
- NEVER remove the quality-first fetch logic — it ensures best content surfaces first
- Room is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH — UI never reads Firestore directly
- Any new sync feature must show reads/day math before implementation
